Subject: [PATCH] feat(jigsaw): translate native block settings and edit
 requests

Preserve both signed priority fields in Java block entity data and translate Java 26.3 jigsaw settings into a complete Bedrock BlockActorData compound. Copy the server snapshot so pending edits do not mutate authoritative state, retain unknown fields, and reject targets that are no longer jigsaw blocks.

Bedrock 1.26.51.1 build 51061372 exposes both priorities and the aligned/rollable joint in its native editor. Reopening preserves negative selection and positive placement priorities. A protocol 2193 server persists a complete BlockActorData request with custom names, replacement state, joint, and both priorities. Jigsaw worldgen rules and structure generation remain separate work.
